notes:
Networking - Basically a group of devices connected together.
Internet - Made up of many small networks connected together.
Private network - Small networks mentioned above.
Public network - The internet so the network connecting these private networks.
IP address (Internet Protocol):
  Made from 4 octets from 0-255 per number for example 192.168.1.1. Comes from 2^8 - 1.
  Used as a way of identifying a host on a network for a period of time.
Media access control (MAC) address:
  Assigned numbering at factory when built.
  Twelve-character hexadecimal number.
  First 6 characters represent the company that made the network interface.
  Last 6 characters are unique numbers.
    Example: a4:c3:f0:85:ac:2d . Also (:) are separators.
Spoofing - Faking a MAC address.
IPv4 - Uses numbering system of 2^32 (4.29 billion).
IPv6 - Uses numbering system of 2^128 (340 trillion-plus).
IPv4 and IPv6 Examples:
  IPv4: 86.157.52.21 .
  IPv6: 2a00:22c4:a531:c500:425f:cce6:c36b:f64d .
Ping - Uses ICMP packets to determine the performance of a connnection between devices. ICMP (Internet Control Message Protocol).
To do a simple ping - ping <Ip address> or <Website url> .

